To find the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in a given string, we can use dynamic programming. The idea is to build a 2D table where `dp[i][j]` represents the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the substring `s[i...j]`. The base case is when the start index is greater than the end index, which means the length is 0, and when the start index is equal to the end index, the length is 1 since a single character is always a palindrome.

